body:
These new tests construct dates with `new Date('YYYY-MM-DD')`, which is parsed as UTC and can display as the previous day in non-UTC timezones when formatted with `toLocaleDateString`, causing flaky failures. Prefer constructing local dates via `new Date(year, monthIndex, day)` or include an explicit time+timezone (e.g. `...T00:00:00Z`) and format with a fixed `timeZone` option.
```suggestion
    start: new Date(2024, 0, 15),
    end: new Date(2024, 1, 15),
    progress: 75,
  },
  {
    id: '2',
    title: 'Development',
    start: new Date(2024, 1, 1),
    end: new Date(2024, 2, 15),
```
